In addition to $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ , $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ and $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ sorption measurements were performed in the low pressure region (0-1 bar) at various temperatures. Accordingly, $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ adsorption at $_{77}\mathrm{K}$ revealed an impressive uptake of $261~\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathbf{g}^{-1}$ (2.3 wt $\%$ ) at 1 bar with a ${\mathrm{~{Q}}_{\mathrm{{st}}}}^{\mathrm{~o}}$ of $6.3\mathrm{kJ\mol^{-1}}$ (see figure S21 and S19). A very high $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ uptake was also found, reaching at 273 K, 298 K and 1 bar, $\mathbf{149~cm^{3}}$ (STP) $\mathbf{g}^{-1}\left(6.6\mathrm{\mmol\g}^{-1}\right)$ and $80~\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathbf{g}^{-1}\left(3.6\mathrm{mmol}\mathrm{g}^{-1}\right)$ , respectively (see figure $\mathrm{S_{17}}\mathrm{\dot{}}$ ). The corresponding $\mathrm{Q}_{\mathrm{st}}$ at zero coverage, determined for the isotherms recorded at 273 K , ${}_{283}\mathrm{~K~}$ and 298 K, is estimated to be 24.5 kJ mol-1 and found to be constant as function of the surface coverage, indicating the presence of uniform $\mathrm{CO}_{2}$ -framework interactions in Cu-tbo-MOF- $^{\cdot5}$ (see figure S18). Using the IAST model, the calculated $\mathrm{CO_{2}/C H_{4}}$ selectivity at $_{273}\mathrm{~K~}$ and $_{298\mathrm{~K~}}$ for a $5/95$ molar mixture is 5.1 and 4.2, respectively (see figure S20).
## CONCLUSIONS
In conclusion, we have demonstrated how reticular chemistry and more specifically the Supermolecular Building Layer (SBL) approach can allow the synthesis of a new series of tbo-MOFs with significantly enhanced gravimetric and volumetric surface area, compared to the prototype tbo MOF, HKUST-1. The design of an original expanded, highly aromatic and rigid organic linkers with intrinsic strong $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ adsorption sites, allowed the isolation of a new very stable porous MOF, namely $\mathtt{C u}$ -tbo$\mathrm{\bfMOF-}5$ that shows very high gravimetric and volumetric BET surface area, reaching 3971 ${\mathfrak{m}}^{2}$ (STP) $\mathbf{g}^{-1}$ and $2363\mathrm{~m}^{2}$ $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ , respectively. Extensive gas adsorption measurements, at various temperatures and pressures, revealed that $\mathtt{C u}$ -tbo-MOF- $5$ is currently among the best performing MOFs for $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ storage, showing a gravimetric total uptake of $372~\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathbf{g}^{-1}$ at $^{85}$ bar and 298 K, which is higher than that in HKUST-1 and MOF-519, and also an impressive volumetric total capacity of 221 $\mathrm{cm}^{3}$ (STP) $\mathrm{cm}^{-3}$ ,
## Journal of the American Chemical Society
under the same conditions (working capacity between 5- 80 bar, $175\ \mathrm{cm}^{3}\ \mathrm{cm}^{-3},$ . Theoretical calculations of the $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ adsorption in Cu-tbo-MOF- $5$ , revealed the presence of multiple strong adsorption sites of equal strength with the open ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ sites $\left({\sim}20\mathrm{~kJ\mol^{-1}}\right)$ , which concurs with the experimentally determined isosteric heat of adsorption. The increased strength of these sites originates from both the particular structural features of the ligand and the tbo-MOF structural features, tbo topology. These significant results provide new directions for the design and construction of novel tbo-MOFs with further improved $\mathrm{CH}_{4}$ storage properties, namely with enhanced volumetric total and working capacities while maintaining a high density of strong interaction sites.
